{
  "_doc": "Audio (story 13.1, services/audioLogic.js, services/Audio.js): all sounds are made on the fly with the Web Audio API, no files. Nothing plays before the first tap or key press (browsers keep the AudioContext asleep until a gesture; the service creates it then) and nothing plays while the family has switched sound off (flag audioMuted, parent settings). At most `voiceCap` sounds play at once; a louder-priority sound cuts the quietest one when full. `sfx`: wave (sine, square, triangle, sawtooth) sweeping f0 to f1 Hz, or `noise` filtered at f0 to f1 Hz, over `dur` seconds at `gain`, `priority` 0-3. `events`: game events and the names of the `sfx:play` hook that map to a sound (names with a sound of their own play it directly). Pitch gets a tiny deterministic variation so repeats do not sound robotic.",
